incident_only_answer:
Based on the incident summary, it appears that a volumetric Denial-of-Service (DoS) attack via HTTP (DDoS_HTTP) is the dominant threat, accounting for 83.69% of anomalies and exhausting shared IoT management resources. To prevent such attacks from occurring in the future, consider implementing infrastructure controls that can mitigate HTTP flood traffic. These may include:

* Configuring rate limiting on IoT devices or network edge to restrict incoming HTTP requests per second;
* Implementing DDoS protection services that can detect and block malicious traffic patterns;
* Using web application firewalls (WAFs) with signature-based detection and IP blocking capabilities; and
* Segmenting networks to limit the spread of DoS attacks.

Additionally, reviewing and implementing security patches for affected IoT devices is crucial. This may include updating firmware or software to address any known vulnerabilities that could be exploited by attackers.

